H6000.def:
A man of the tribe of Asher living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 7:35; 
son of: Hotham (H2369); 
brother of: Zophah (H6690), Imna (H3234) and Shelesh (H8028) 
§ Amal = "labour"
an Asherite, son of Helem

H6002H.def:
A man of the Edomites living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 36:12; 
son of: Eliphaz (H0464) and Timna (H8555); 
brother of: Teman (H8487), Omar (H0201), Zepho (H6825), Gatam (H1609), Kenaz (H7073) and Korah (H7141H)
§ Amalek = "dweller in a valley"
1) son of Eliphaz by his concubine Timnah, grandson of Esau, and progenitor of a tribe of people in southern Canaan
2) descendants of Amalek

H6005.def:
A man living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at Ésaïe 7:14; 
son of: Joseph (G2501) and Mary (G3137); 
brother of: James (G2385I), Joseph (G2500), Simon (G4613H) and Jude (G2455I)
Also named: Emmanouēl (Ἐμμανουήλ "Immanuel" G1694) 
§ Immanuel = "God with us" or "with us is God"
symbolic and prophetic name of the Messiah, the Christ, prophesying that He would be born of a virgin and would be 'God with us'

H6019G.def:
A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Exode 6:18; 
son of: Kohath (H6955); 
brother of: Izhar (H3324), Hebron (H2275B) and Uzziel (H5816); married to Jochebed (H3115); 
father of: Moses (H4872), Aaron (H0175) and Miriam (H4813)
Also named: am.ra.mi (עַמְרָמִי "Amramite" H6020)
§ Amram = "exalted people"
1) a descendant of Kohath and Levi and father of Moses
2) one of the sons of Bani who had a foreign wife in the time of Ezra

H6020.def:
Someone descended from Amram who was a man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Exode 6:18; 
son of: Kohath (H6955); 
brother of: Izhar (H3324), Hebron (H2275B) and Uzziel (H5816); married to Jochebed (H3115); 
father of: Moses (H4872), Aaron (H0175) and Miriam (H4813)
Group of am.ram (עַמְרָם "Amram" H6019) 
§ Amramites, of Aram "exalted"
a branch of the Kohathite family of the tribe of Levi and descendants of Amram, the father of Moses

H6023.def:
A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of Exile and Return, first mentioned at 1 Chroniques 9:12; 
son of: Adiel (H5717H); also called Amashsai (KJV: Amashai) at Néhémie 11:13; 
Another name of ma.a.say (מַעֲשַׂי "Maasai" H4640) 
§ Amashai = "burdensome"
a priest, son of Azareel in the time of Nehemiah

H6036.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 4:8; 
son of: Koz (H6976); 
brother of: Zobebah (H6637) and Harum (H2037) 
§ Anub = "confederate"
son of Coz, descendant of Judah and Caleb through Ashur, the father of Tekoa

H6054.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 3:24; 
son of: Elioenai (H0454B); 
brother of: Hodaviah (H1938), Eliashib (H0475), Pelaiah (H6411B), Akkub (H6126), Johanan (H3110I) and Delaiah (H1806) 
§ Anani = "my cloud"
the 7th son of Elioenai, descendant of David

H6061.def:
A man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Nombres 13:22; 
father of: Ahiman (H0289), Sheshai (H8344) and Talmai (H8526); also called Anakim at Deutéronome 1:28; 2.10,11,21; 9.2; 1x,22; 14.12,15;
Also named: a.na.qi (עֲנָקִי "Anakim" H6062) 
§ Anak = "neck"
progenitor of a family, or tribe of the giant people in Canaan

H6062.def:
Someone descended from Anak who was a man living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Nombres 13:22; 
father of: Ahiman (H0289), Sheshai (H8344) and Talmai (H8526); also called Anakim at Deutéronome 1:28; 2.10,11,21; 9.2; 1x,22; 14.12,15;
Group of a.naq (עֲנָק "Anak" H6061) 
§ Anakims = "long-necked"
a tribe of giants, descendants of Anak, which dwelled in southern Canaan

H6070.def:
A man of the tribe of Benjamin living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 8:24; 
son of: Shashak (H8349); 
brother of: Ishpan (H3473), Eber (H5677J), Eliel (H0447I), Abdon (H5658I), Zichri (H2147I), Hanan (H2605), Hananiah (H2608O), Elam (H5867), Iphdeiah (H3301) and Penuel (H6439I) 
§ Antothijah = "Jehovah's answer"
a Benjamite, one of the sons of Jeroham

H6085I.def:
A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 41:52; 
son of: Joseph (H3130) and Asenath (H0621); 
brother of: Manasseh (H4519); 
father of: Shuthelah (H7803), Becher (H1071H), Tahan (H8465), Ezer (H5827), Elead (H0496) and Beriah (H1283H); also called Ephrathite (NIV: Ephraimite) at 1 Samuel 1:1; Ephron (Qere, KJV: Ephrain) at 2 Chroniques 13:19; 
Another name of eph.ra.yim (אֶפְרַ֫יִם "Ephraim" H0669G)
§ Ephron = "fawn-like"
1) a Hittite, son of Zohar and the one from whom Abraham bought the field and cave of Machpelah
2) a city on the borders of Benjamin
3) a mountain on the northern border of Judah
